AB  - This paper provides a strategy that controls the formation of platoons while driving and keeps up the target formation. Before reaching destinations, platoons can be affected by unpredictable factors such as an error in wireless communication, malfunctioning sensors, and weather conditions. These factors result in the transformation of platoons’ formations and their shape would be randomly determined. Therefore, this paper focuses on returning to the target formation from the change of the formation that is randomly determined while minimizing energy consumption. To consider this randomness, unpredictable factors are set as a variable that can affect the formation, and a mathematical model with the purpose of minimum energy consumption is developed. Furthermore, safety for vehicle platoons should be considered when platooning. To consider it, penalties of velocity that determine the gap between adjacent vehicles are added to the developed model. To find the most proper method for the application to the real world, simulations are conducted by proposing three algorithms suitable for CPLEX, stochastic dynamic game, and reinforcement learning based on the developed mathematical model. As a result, it is observed that the model solved by CPLEX always has the best solution, however, the model by CPLEX is not suitable since its computation time takes longer than the time that the velocity of vehicles should be determined. In the meantime, it is discovered that the reinforcement learning model out of the other two shows a better performance of energy consumption reduction and safety through the results of simulations. © 2025 Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.
