AB  - This work presents a reinforcement learning method of generating discrete skills while evolving environments in a system. We present a method for determining when to create new skills, how to characterize unknown skills and expand both the actual capability and confidence in these abilities for a reinforcement learning agent. We provide an example wherein many diverse environments for the Bipedal Walker are generated using Uber's POET (Paired Open-Ended Trailblazer) and are then combined with an example world model to derive a relatively small library of skills capable of solving most generated environments. The skills-based approach solves over 85% of the solvable generated environments with an 80-fold reduction in the number of policies required and an exponential reduction in CPU hours used for training. © 2024 IEEE.
