AB  - Over the years many techniques have been used by the decision makers to test their theories in a near real world simulated situation. Military war games are one such platform where these theories can be tested and the outcome is recorded. War gaming has evolved from its starting as a board game to now widely played as a computer game. This paper focuses on a military war game simulation which is being used to develop a bot using artificial intelligence techniques. Various modules are developed for working of the bot. Route planning is one of them which is used by units to find a path in the game. Thus, an algorithm is proposed using the A* algorithm as a base. A* algorithm is modified to use influence maps in order to find a safe path for the units which helps the bot succeed in the game. The modified A* algorithm is implemented and compared with a traditional A* algorithm and modified algorithm is found to be more optimal. © Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2018.
