AB  - This paper proposes an architecture for implementing 'Spatial AI' that enables autonomous agents to systematically imagine and navigate their environment. Spatial AI, when implemented, allows for the prediction of the state of the world and the generation of the behavior of the group of agents. A digital twin of a dynamic collective agent environment, including autonomous groups of agents, serves as a basis for simulating various situations and actions. As a means of implementing this architecture, the SSCP Model is proposed, which is a framework for artificial intelligence that can manage agents existing within an arbitrary space. By unifying the agents' communication style, spatial intelligence, spatial representation, and environmental knowledge, Spatial AI provides a Common Ground for controlling diverse groups of AI agents.  © 2023 IEEE.
