AB  - Until recently, efficient policy iteration algorithms for zero-sum Markov games that converge were unknown. Therefore, model-based RL algorithms for such problems could not use policy iteration in the planning modules of the algorithms. In an earlier paper, we showed that a convergent policy iteration algorithm can be obtained by using a commonly used technique in RL called lookahead. However, the algorithm could be applied to the function approximation setting only in the special case of linear MDPs (Markov Decision Processes). In this paper, we obtain performance bounds for policy-based RL algorithms for general settings, including one where policy evaluation is performed using noisy samples of (state, action, reward) triplets from a single sample path of a given policy.  © 2023 IEEE.
