AB  - Autonomous vehicles are becoming prevalent in the modern world. Such vehicles either require little or no manual intervention during their operation. However, setting up test scenarios for autonomous vehicles in the real world is a complicated task and has real-world implications in the form of damage to the vehicle itself and damage to public property. Neither industry nor authorities have settled on a standard procedure to carry out tests. Meanwhile, autonomous vehicle tests carried out in a simulation will be much safer. Virtual tests may be re-run countless times, and the data from these tests may be used to create new and unforeseen abstract test scenarios. This research work trains the neural networks AlexNet, AlexNet V2 and InceptionResNet V3 to learn to drive a car in a detailed and diverse simulated world. © 2023 IEEE.
