TI  - DURABLE-RL: A Dynamic Uncertainty-aware Hybrid Reinforcement Learning Framework with Adaptive Buffer and Ensemble Modelling
PY  - 2025
T2  - International Journal of Intelligent Engineering and Systems
VL  - 18
IS  - 9
SP  - 494
EP  - 509
DO  - 10.22266/ijies2025.1031.32
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105018512403?origin=resultslist
AB  - Reinforcement Learning (RL) systems have proved their abilities to accomplish multi-stage decisionmaking processes. Nevertheless, effectiveness in utilizing samples still poses a serious concern for practical scenarios. This paper presents DURABLE-RL (Dynamic Uncertainty-aware Reinforcement Learning with Adaptive Buffer and Ensemble), an enhanced hybrid RL architecture that combines model-based and model-free approaches towards improving sample efficiency, while simultaneously achieving optimal policy execution. First, the framework employs an uncertainty-aware switching mechanism that adjusts the mix of real and synthetic training episodes according to how confident it is in the learned transition function. Second, a multi-scale ensemble of models is used to reduce the accumulation of errors during long-horizon rollouts. Third, a hybrid experience replay buffer prioritizes real interactions whenever uncertainty peaks, thereby stabilizing the overall learning process. To evaluate this approach, an extensive testing was performed against RL algorithms such as Soft Actor-Critic (SAC), Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO), Model-Based Policy Optimization (MBPO), DreamerV2, MuZero, and other competing methods on MuJoCo and Atari datasets benchmarks, which comprise continuous control as well as high-dimensional visual environments, are well known simulated RL testbeds. The testing results indicate that DURABLE-RL is able to achieve over 91.2% accuracy with 89.8% recall and 90.5% F1 score, which are outstanding compared to other approaches. In addition, the framework achieves sample efficiency improvements of over 21% and 9% against LSTMRL and PSDRL respectively, while achieving the highest cumulative reward of 2650. The results verify that the DURABLE-RL facilitates faster convergence, improved sample efficiency, and ensures strong performance in various RL scenarios. © This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License. License details: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
