AB  - Real-time rendering plays a crucial role in interactive applications such as video games, simulations, and virtual reality (VR), where achieving high visual fidelity while maintaining optimal performance is key. This paper investigates the integration of DirectX12 (DX12) within Unreal Engine to enhance real-time rendering efficiency. DirectX12, a low-level graphics API, provides developers with explicit control over hardware resources, improving GPU utilization, reducing CPU overhead, and supporting advanced techniques like multi-threading and resource management. The combination of DX12's capabilities and Unreal Engine's rendering pipeline allows for the optimization of dynamic scenes, complex shaders, and large-scale environments. This study not only explores the technical benefits for gaming and VR applications but also emphasizes the interdisciplinary nature of optimizing hardware, software, and graphics technologies for high-performance rendering. Through performance evaluations, it is demonstrated that DX12 improves frame rates, reduces latency, and enhances visual quality, contributing significantly to modern interactive applications across various fields. © 2025 IOS Press.
